<p>This is one of those bizarre ideas I believe definitely belongs on this site at some point. I love the creativity and thought that you put into this. I know this is just an idea critique forum, but if you're seeking green light, my suggestion to you would be to work on your clinical tone and your grammar. For example, &quot;Weirdly enough, it has no body parts except for limbs and the torso, and head. The bottom of its feet where you would usually find paws, is just more fur.&quot; This could be written in a way that makes it stronger, &quot;The entity posses all four limbs, but lacks extremities such as paws. Instead the legs end in stubs, balanced on balled up, matted fur. The entity also lacks any visible orifices, or genitalia. This implies the anomaly lacks any digestive track or endocrine system typical of a domesticated canine.&quot;</p>
<p>Because the idea is so bizarre and frankly a little funny/cute, I think the best way to get this SCP ready for green light is to rework your idea presentation. Show us you can make this idea draft work in that clinical tone as best as possible to amplify the strengths of your idea.</p>
